npm/README.md:77:cd ceo-orchestration
npm/README.md:87:> **Install paths.** The clone-and-`install.sh` flow above is the supported path today. A one-step npm shim is also available — `npx ceo-orchestration /path/to/your-app` (published to npm with SLSA **Level 2** provenance via `npm publish --provenance`; Level 3 is out of scope — see `npm/INTEGRITY.md`).
npm/README.md:114:/path/to/ceo-orchestration/scripts/uninstall.sh /path/to/your-app
npm/README.md:139:- **Per-edit overhead.** Each governed tool call runs the hook chain before the action lands, adding roughly **~0.3–1.0s** of latency per edit on typical hardware. That is the cost of the gate; if you want zero overhead on routine work, the governance layer is not free.
npm/README.md:144:- **No speed benefit.** Restated because it matters: this will not make your agent faster.
