.claude/settings.json:2:  "_comment": "CEO Orchestration — local settings for THIS repo (ceo-orchestration itself). Source of truth for distribution lives in templates/settings/ (settings.base.json + settings.stack.<name>.json). This file is a dogfooded BASE install — no tsc/vitest pre-commit gate because this repo has no TypeScript.",
.claude/settings.json:301:        "_comment": "PLAN-083 Wave 0a sub-agent 0.5: anti-CEO-overhead detector. PreToolUse hook detecting CEO doing work a sub-agent could do equally well (P1 sequential skill reads / P2 unrelated edits / P3 serial schema authoring / P4 grep/find serial / P5 cross-module test writes). Fail-OPEN on infra bug. Emit budget ≤20/day. Override CEO_OVERHEAD_ACK=1. Kill-switch CEO_ANTI_OVERHEAD=0. p95 latency ≤50ms (bench 0.029ms). PLAN-125 WS-1 (kooky-harvest): matcher widened to the broad tool set so this hook also writes the cheap per-tool-call PreToolUse lifecycle stamp (tool_use_id pairing record; emits NO audit-chain event per MF-SEC-5) co-located here to add NO new subprocess (MF-PERF-1). Lifecycle kill-switch CEO_TOOL_LIFECYCLE=0.",
.claude/settings.json:306:            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\" check_anti_ceo_overhead.py",
.claude/settings.json:308:            "statusMessage": "Checking for CEO-overhead anti-patterns..."
.claude/settings.json:325:        "_comment": "PLAN-125 WS-2 (kooky-harvest) — parallel-writer worktree-isolation enforcement. Default-OFF: INERT unless the writer self-sets CEO_PARALLEL_WRITER=1 (+ CEO_ASSIGNED_WORKTREE=<abs>). When ACTIVE it is UNCONDITIONAL + fail-CLOSED — DENIES any Bash/Edit/Write/MultiEdit whose RESOLVED target lands in the shared main checkout instead of the assigned dedicated worktree (ADR-049a AMEND-1; stops the S191 worktree-bleed). cwd resolved at the PreToolUse decision point (no TOCTOU via a later cd/git -C — MF-SEC-6); git refs/paths require a `--` end-of-options separator + allowlist regex (MF-SEC-7). Fail-OPEN only on an infra/parse bug of the hook itself. INFRA for non-conflicting parallel reads/reviews — NO throughput/speed claim (MF-4).",
.claude/settings.json:363:        "_comment": "Silent audit-log observer (Python): appends one JSONL line per Agent spawn to $HOME/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration/audit-log.jsonl. Emits nothing on stdout (composes with reminder hook). Schema: .claude/plans/AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md. Adds hook_duration_ms field + monthly rotation at 10MB.",
.claude/settings.json:375:        "_comment": "Confidence gate (Sprint 9 Phase 1, ADR-019): PostToolUse Agent hook that invokes confidence_gate.py CLI over agent output, emits confidence_gate audit event, and ENFORCES blocking when CEO_CONFIDENCE_ENFORCE=1 (Owner-only flip; see ADR-019 + RELEASE.md). Advisory-only by default. CEO_CONFIDENCE_BYPASS=1 is the session-scoped escape hatch. Fail-open on timeout/infra per CLAUDE.md §Critical Rules. 10s timeout covers the CLI's 5s subprocess + overhead.",
.claude/settings.json:721:        "_comment": "PLAN-135 W2 H8: Setup-event post-install self-verification (init matcher) — validate-governance --fast + verify-counts + hook exec-bits (the S228 exec-bit class) + CLAUDE_ENV_FILE allowlist persistence (explicit CEO_* include-list; every override/escape-hatch/kill-switch EXCLUDED, S185/S197 stale-override class). ADVISORY + fail-open; NEVER blocks. Kill-switch: CEO_SETUP_VERIFICATION=0.",
