SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:328:| `pair_rail_case` (v2.23) | `action`, `case` (str — closed enum: `A` / `B` / `C` / `D` / `E` / `F` per spec.md §11 asymmetric matrix), `claude_verdict` (str — closed enum: `PASS` / `BLOCK`), `codex_verdict` (str — closed enum: `PASS` / `BLOCK` / `ADVISORY` / `TIMEOUT` / `MALFORMED`), `tool_name` (str ≤32 — closed enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty) PER-INVOCATION correlation id, PLAN-161 W2 C5 r5 F2: minted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at review entry (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and IDENTICAL on this case emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_review_expected` — the invocation correlation key the /ceo-boot `failopen_rail_liveness_7d` expected/terminal pairing matches on; off-shape COERCED to empty in the typed wrapper AND the `emit_generic` dispatch branch (r6 F2: the RAW value is validated — any other length incl. oversize, uppercase or non-hex is DROPPED, never truncated, so two distinct off-shape ids sharing a 16-hex prefix can never alias to one pairing key); empty = legacy/id-less emit, paired via the (session, file-hash) bucket-count fallback), `precondition_met` (bool — Case-B requires file:line cited + rubric_violation_id ∈ catalogue + severity ∈ {P0, P1}), `rubric_violation_id` (str ≤64 — enumerated ID from `.claude/policies/rubric-violation-catalogue.yaml` or empty when not Case-B; free-form rubric IDs are sanitized to `unknown_rubric_id`), `severity` (str — closed enum: `P0` / `P1` / empty), `jaccard_similarity_bucket` (str — closed enum: `<=0.3` / `0.3-0.5` / `0.5-0.8` / `>0.8` / empty; raw float forbidden per Sec MF-3), `human_triage_grace_h` (int ≥0 — hours remaining in 24h grace window per R1 S-TDE-4; 0 = grace expired = closes-as-advisory; CEO_PAIR_RAIL_HUMAN_TRIAGE_HOURS env override), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget this invocation ran under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Purpose is §4(i): before this field a case F produced by a sub-floor `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S` export was byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage, which made the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented kill-switch. Encoding is load-bearing, not stylistic: a float in an HMAC-covered field is rejected by `_lib/canonical_json.py` and the spool writer then DROPS THE WHOLE EVENT with only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb — for this action that would manufacture the very /ceo-boot liveness deficit `review_id` exists to disprove), `session_id`, `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline HMAC-chain invariant. PLAN-081 Phase 3 (S100 ceremony 2026-05-10) — emitted by `.claude/hooks/check_pair_rail.py:_decide_with_matrix()` once per Pair-Rail PreToolUse evaluation that reaches the matrix arm (write tool + L3+ path + no sentinel bypass). Source action for `fp_rate_30d` and `disagreement_rate_30d` predicate aggregators. ADR-107 + ADR-108 ACCEPTED gate. Sec MF-3 invariant: NEVER persist raw Codex review body / proposed-content / file path. Registered with `KERNEL_OVERRIDE` bypass since `audit_emit.py` is in `_KERNEL_PATHS`. |
