SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:495:| `pair_rail_review_expected` (v2.52) | `action`, `tool_name` (str — CLOSED enum: `Edit` / `Write` / `MultiEdit` / `NotebookEdit` / `unknown`; off-enum COERCED to `unknown`), `file_path_hash_prefix` (str — 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of target file path, the SAME token/helper as `pair_rail_case`; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to empty; raw path forbidden per LLM06 side-channel guard; r4 F2, retained as the LEGACY fallback bucket key + harmless secondary key — id-less events still pair per (session, file-hash) BUCKET), `review_id` (str — exact-shape `([0-9a-f]{16})?` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex, or empty; r6 F2: raw value validated, off-shape incl. oversize DROPPED to empty — never truncated); r5 F2 — THE invocation correlation key: minted per review entry by `_decide()` (`os.urandom(8).hex()`) and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`, so the /ceo-boot deficit pairs a specific expected with its OWN case — counting (even (session, file-hash)-bucketed) cannot: an old completed case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1. An EXPECTED `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window = an outstanding (dead) review -> RED; off-shape COERCED to empty; empty falls back to the bucket-count heuristic (best-effort, pre-land events only — post-land every review carries an id)), `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the paired review runs under, in integer MILLISECONDS, NOT float seconds; canonical_json no-float invariant, same encoding as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` — divide by 1000 to recover seconds; off-shape/NaN/inf/bool COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget", bounded in the typed wrapper AND re-coerced in the `emit_generic` dispatch branch. Carried on the DENOMINATOR as well as the case so the pair records the budget it ran under even when the case never arrives — see the `pair_rail_case` row for the §4(i) rationale and for why the integer encoding is load-bearing), `session_id` (explicit required kwarg on the typed emitter — the hook threads the PreToolUse event's own session id, no silent default), `project`, `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 (2026-07-27) — canonical-edit review ENTERED marker, emitted by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` only after the kill-switch / non-write-tool / not-L3+ / sentinel-bypass arms have all returned (those paths emit NOTHING). The durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail` activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and escalates RED; zero expected + zero outcomes is vacuously green; a healthy outcome from session B never masks session A. Typed emitter `emit_pair_rail_review_expected`; dedicated deny-by-default `_PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch + closed-enum coercion, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: file paths, proposed content, any review text. NO ATLAS technique (liveness telemetry, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:529:| `subagent_lifecycle_observed` (v2.43) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `agent_archetype` (str — CLOSED enum, persona-ledger archetype: `code-reviewer` / `security-engineer` / `qa-architect` / `threat-detection-engineer` / `other` / `unknown`; coerced to `other`), `wall_bucket` (str — CLOSED bucket enum: `none` / `low` / `medium` / `high` / `very_high` / `unknown`; coerced to `unknown`), `wall_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `bracketed` / `unknown`; coerced to `unknown`), `token_bucket` (str — same CLOSED bucket enum; coerced to `unknown`), `claim_bucket` (str — same CLOSED bucket enum; coerced to `unknown`), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-135 W2 H3 (anthropic-surface-harvest) — per-agent SubagentStop lifecycle bracket: emitted ONCE per returning sub-agent by `check_fluency_nudge.py` (the SubagentStop H3 extension) after consuming the SubagentStart sidecar written by `check_subagent_start.py` (keyed `sha256(agent_id)[:16]`, popped on read) + the harness-supplied `agent_transcript_path` (line/byte/wall-bounded; only integer usage fields read; realpath-under-`$HOME/.claude` containment). The S227 `modelUsage` forensic reconstruction becomes a live hook emit; feeds the persona-ledger (PLAN-104) via `agent_archetype`. `wall_bucket` is the stop-instant minus the recorded `start_ts` (bracketed; `wall_source=unknown` when the start was never recorded). `token_bucket` brackets the SUM of `input_tokens + output_tokens + cache_creation_input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens` across the transcript. `claim_bucket` brackets the confidence-marker count the hook already computes. Producer: `.claude/hooks/check_fluency_nudge.py` via the TYPED wrapper `emit_subagent_lifecycle_observed`. Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_SUBAGENT_LIFECYCLE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the RAW token counts, the RAW wall-time seconds, the transcript path/body, the confidence-marker snippets and the raw agent_id — only the closed-enum archetype + the four coarse brackets travel (the bracket is the audit signal; the raw counts stay forensic-private). Kill-switch: `CEO_SUBAGENT_LIFECYCLE=0` (shared by the SubagentStart recorder + this SubagentStop consumer). NO ATLAS technique (governance/accounting breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:586:| v2.55 | ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6 (pair-rail timeout recalibration 120/150 → 180/210 s, S291 ceremony 2026-08-03) — NO new action (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` stays 324) and no new allowlist. ONE new bounded field `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the invocation ran under) added to the EXISTING `pair_rail_case` AND `pair_rail_review_expected` allowlists, coerced in both typed wrappers AND both `emit_generic` dispatch branches (never `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`). Motivation is the §4(i) named residual: no event recorded the effective budget, so a session exporting `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S=5` produced a case F byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage — making the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE` kill-switch, which emits its own loud event. A minimum floor on the knob stays DEFERRED (changing a documented knob's semantics is a new contract, AMEND-1 consensus item 2), but the incentive gradient is no longer inverted and the next amendment's historical series is no longer born ambiguous. **Encoding is normative, not stylistic:** MILLISECONDS as an int, NOT the float seconds the amendment prose names — `_lib/canonical_json.py` rejects floats in HMAC-covered fields, and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb, which on these two actions would manufacture the exact /ceo-boot S254 liveness deficit they exist to measure. Same encoding + rationale as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` (PLAN-081 Phase 2, Codex iter 1 P0-1). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. | *(1 new bounded int field on 2 existing actions; no new actions, no new allowlists; shared coercion `_coerce_pair_rail_timeout_ms` + bound `_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX` in `audit_emit.py`)* |
