   564	      # PLAN-166 F4 (OQ-4) - install/upgrade parity on the RESULTING TREES,
   565	      # per ceremony mode. NO continue-on-error, deliberately: the assertion
   566	      # this replaces was dead twice over (tautological AND wired into no
   567	      # workflow), and an escape hatch here would reinstate exactly that.
   568	      # Exit 2 (KNOWN-OPEN) is a FAILURE too - it NAMES the outstanding
   569	      # PLAN-166 W1 prerequisites instead of skipping them silently.
   570	      - name: Install/upgrade parity e2e (maintainer + user ceremony)
   571	        run: |
   572	          set -euo pipefail
   573	          bash scripts/tests/test-install-upgrade-parity-e2e.sh
   574	
   575	      # Control of the control (AC-4). With ONE backup_and_replace line deleted
   576	      # from a COPY of upgrade.sh, the gate above must come back RED in EVERY
   577	      # ceremony mode. rc must be exactly 1: rc 0/2 means the gate went blind,
   578	      # rc 9 means the plant stopped biting (vacuous control). Both fail here.
   579	      # This step MUST stay AFTER the plain gate: if the un-planted run were
   580	      # already fatal, rc=1 here would prove nothing about the plant.
   581	      # PLAN-183 W5 (§9.8) — `if: always()`. Observed in run 32639637945: with
   582	      # the main parity step FAILING (D1 open), this control and the two steps
   583	      # below all reported `skipped`. That is the worst possible moment to
   584	      # lose them: the control is the step that answers "does the classifier
   585	      # still DETECT a planted divergence?", so a later green main step would
   586	      # be certified by an instrument whose detection power was never
   587	      # re-verified in the same run — the "instrumento verde cuja PERGUNTA
   588	      # envelheceu" class. The Check: in a run with the main step RED, this
   589	      # step must report success or failure, NEVER skipped.
   590	      # TRADE-OFF, deliberate: always() also runs on a CANCELLED job (an
   591	      # operator cancel, or the job-level timeout, which surfaces as a cancel).
   592	      # `!cancelled()` would exclude that case; always() is what PLAN-183 §9.8
   593	      # specifies, and the cost is bounded by the job timeout below.
   594	      - name: Install/upgrade parity - positive control (planted divergence)
   595	        if: always()
   596	        run: |
   597	          set -uo pipefail
   598	          rc=0
   599	          bash scripts/tests/test-install-upgrade-parity-e2e.sh \
   600	            --positive-control > /tmp/parity-control.log 2>&1 || rc=$?
   601	          if [ "$rc" -ne 1 ]; then
   602	            cat /tmp/parity-control.log
   603	            echo "::error::parity positive control returned rc=$rc, expected 1 - the planted install/upgrade divergence did NOT turn the gate red, so the gate above proves nothing"
   604	            exit 1
   605	          fi
   606	          # Second factor, LOAD-BEARING (re-pass closure): under `set -uo
   607	          # pipefail` (no -e) a non-matching grep would NOT fail the step, so
   608	          # an rc=1 from a failure UNRELATED to the plant (log with none of
   609	          # the plant markers) would pass — the registered-vacuous class
   610	          # (S292) this step exists to close. Demand plant evidence or fail.
   611	          # PLAN-169 W3.2 (fecha a exceção nomeada do AC-4 do PLAN-166,
   612	          # achado r6-P2): o fator antigo aceitava evidência NÃO-causal —
   613	          # qualquer um dos 3 marcadores, mesmo sem o controle ter
   614	          # DISPARADO. Exigir a linha que só existe quando o plante
   615	          # disparou em TODOS os modos, e nenhum veredito por modo :0/:2.
   616	          { grep -qF 'positive control: FIRED in every mode' /tmp/parity-control.log \
   617	            && ! grep -E 'per-mode verdicts.*:(0|2)' /tmp/parity-control.log >/dev/null; } || {
   618	            cat /tmp/parity-control.log
   619	            echo "::error::rc=1 but the log carries no PLANTED/per-mode-verdict evidence - the control went red for an unrelated reason, which proves nothing about the plant (vacuous control)"
   620	            exit 1
   621	          }
   622	          echo "positive control OK: planted divergence -> exit 1 in every ceremony mode"
