     1	"""Typed event emitters for audit-log.jsonl event stream v2.
     2	
     3	Promotes audit-log.jsonl from single-event-type (`agent_spawn`) to a
     4	typed event stream with discriminator field `action` covering spawns,
     5	debate rounds, plan transitions, veto triggers, benchmark runs, and
     6	lesson writes. See PLAN-004 Phase 1 + ADR-005.
     7	
     8	## Design contract
     9	
    10	- **Additive only.** v1 `agent_spawn` entries remain valid; no fields
    11	  removed. `event_schema: "v2"` field marks new entries. Consumers
    12	  tolerate unknown fields per AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md §2 forward-compat.
    13	- **Fail-open.** Any emission error writes breadcrumb to `audit-log.errors`
    14	  and returns silently. Framework MUST NOT block on observability.
    15	- **Concurrent-write safe.** Uses `_lib.filelock.FileLock` (same lock
    16	  file as `audit_log.py`).
    17	- **Redaction.** Free-text fields (`desc_preview`, `reason_preview`)
    18	  pass through `_lib.redact.redact_secrets` before write.
    19	- **Stdlib-only.** No new dependencies.
    20	
    21	## Public API (pure functions)
    22	
    23	    emit_debate_event(plan_id, round, phase, agent, artifact_path, ...)
    24	    emit_plan_transition(plan_id, from_status, to_status, file_path, ...)
    25	    emit_veto_triggered(hook, reason_code, reason_preview, blocked_tool, ...)
    26	    emit_benchmark_run(benchmark_id, skill, pass_rate, median_score, ...)
    27	    emit_lesson_write(lesson_id, archetype, scope_tags, trigger, ...)
    28	
    29	All emitters are side-effect-only (return None). Unit tests use
    30	`TestEnvContext` from `_lib.testing` for isolation.
    31	
    32	## Reserved fields (writer-deferred)
    33	
    34	Every v2 event reserves nullable `tokens_in`, `tokens_out`, `tokens_total`
