 10085	def emit_pair_rail_review_expected(
 10086	    *,
 10087	    session_id: str,
 10088	    tool_name: str = "unknown",
 10089	    file_path_hash_prefix: str = "",
 10090	    review_id: str = "",
 10091	    timeout_ms: int = 0,
 10092	    project: str = "",
 10093	) -> None:
 10094	    """Emit pair_rail_review_expected (PLAN-161 W2 C5 / CF-9 denominator).
 10095	
 10096	    Fired by `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at the point a canonical-edit
 10097	    Codex review is definitely ENTERED — only after the kill-switch,
 10098	    non-write-tool, not-L3+ and sentinel-bypass arms have all returned. It is
 10099	    the durable session-correlated DENOMINATOR for the /ceo-boot `pair_rail`
 10100	    activity-conditioned liveness row: a window session with
 10101	    expected-but-no-outcome is the S254 dead-rail class and must escalate,
 10102	    and a healthy outcome from session B must never mask session A
 10103	    (`session_id` is therefore an explicit required kwarg — the hook threads
 10104	    the Stop/PreToolUse event's own session id, not a default).
 10105	
 10106	    r5 F2 + r6 F2: `review_id` (EXACTLY 16 lowercase hex or exactly "";
 10107	    the RAW value is validated BEFORE any bounding — off-shape incl.
 10108	    oversize is DROPPED to "", never truncated, so two distinct off-shape
 10109	    ids sharing a 16-hex prefix can never alias to one pairing key) is
 10110	    the PER-INVOCATION correlation key — minted by
 10111	    `check_pair_rail.py:_decide()` at review entry (`os.urandom(8).hex()`)
 10112	    and identical on this emit and the same invocation's `pair_rail_case`.
 10113	    It is what makes the /ceo-boot pairing invocation-EXACT: counting
 10114	    (even the r4 (session, file-hash) BUCKET counting) fundamentally
 10115	    cannot pair a specific expected with its OWN case — an old completed
 10116	    case for the SAME (session, file) offset a later dead expected 1:1.
 10117	    An expected `review_id` with no matching `pair_rail_case` in-window is
 10118	    an outstanding (dead) review -> RED.
 10119	
 10120	    r4 F2 (retained as legacy fallback + harmless secondary key):
 10121	    `file_path_hash_prefix` (the SAME 16-hex SHA-256 path-prefix
 10122	    token `pair_rail_case` carries, computed by the hook with the same
 10123	    helper; bounded shape `[0-9a-f]{0,16}`, off-shape COERCED to "") keys
 10124	    the /ceo-boot expected/terminal pairing per (session, file-hash)
 10125	    BUCKET for id-less (pre-land / fail-open no-id) events only.
 10126	
 10127	    ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6: `timeout_ms` is the EFFECTIVE post-clamp codex
 10128	    budget the paired review ran under, as INTEGER MILLISECONDS (bounded
 10129	    `[0, 6_000_000]`, off-shape COERCED to 0 = "unknown budget"). It is
 10130	    NOT float seconds: `canonical_json` forbids floats in HMAC-covered
 10131	    fields, and the failure is not benign — the spool writer drops the
 10132	    WHOLE event with only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb, which for
 10133	    these two actions would manufacture the very /ceo-boot liveness
 10134	    deficit they exist to measure. Same encoding + rationale as
 10135	    `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms`; divide by 1000 to recover seconds.
 10136	    Its purpose is §4(i): before it existed, a session exporting
 10137	    `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S=5` produced a case F byte-indistinguishable
 10138	    from a genuine Codex outage — the quiet knob was stealthier than the
 10139	    documented kill-switch.
 10140	
 10141	    Deny-by-default: the ONLY caller fields are `session_id` + the
 10142	    closed-enum `tool_name` (off-enum COERCED to "unknown") + the bounded
 10143	    `file_path_hash_prefix` + the bounded `review_id` + the bounded
 10144	    integer `timeout_ms`. Raw file paths and
 10145	    content bodies are NEVER persisted. Fail-open per audit_emit contract.
 10146	    NEVER routes through _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH.
 10147	    """
 10148	    safe_tool = (
 10149	        tool_name
 10150	        if tool_name in _PAIR_RAIL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_TOOL_ENUM
 10151	        else "unknown"
 10152	    )
 10153	    _raw_prefix = (file_path_hash_prefix or "")[:16]
