   102	### Security — delivered-template destinations are confined to the target (PLAN-185, ADR-196)
   103	
   104	- **`install.sh` wrote outside `$TARGET`** when a destination path was a
   105	  pending symlink or hardlink. One destination-confinement predicate now
   106	  lives in `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh`; `install.sh` pre-flies
   107	  every delivered-template destination before the first write and
   108	  refuses by name, `upgrade.sh` consumes the same predicate. E2E in
   109	  bytes: 105/0 after the cure against 22/33 before it (`cc00235`).
   110	  Several seams stay outside that preflight in this release candidate
   111	  and are signed conditions of rc.1: the `state/mcp_client_secrets`
   112	  seed (a symlinked `TARGET/state` is followed by `mkdir -p`/`chmod`);
   113	  a refused SOURCE template (symlink outside the checkout) that install
   114	  reports as `SKIP` and upgrade as `PRESERVED` while still exiting 0; a
   115	  source MISSING from the executing checkout (`SKIP`, exit 0, on both
   116	  install and upgrade); the `.gitignore`/`.claude/.gitignore` appends,
   117	  which test `-L` only, so a hard link there is written through; the
   118	  `.claude/dispatcher/` copies, which run no check at all (a symlink or a
   119	  hard link there is written through); and `install_dispatcher`, which
   120	  re-copies unconditionally on a rerun (edited dispatcher files are
   121	  overwritten — back them up first); and the deny-baseline merge of
   122	  `install.sh`, which writes a PID-named sibling of `.claude/settings.json`
   123	  outside the preflight (a pre-placed symlink there is written through —
   124	  the `find` check over `.claude/` in `docs/UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md` catches
   125	  it; run it before a fresh install too).
   126	- **`--github-owner` with a `/` in it left `.github/CODEOWNERS` at zero
   127	  bytes, permanently.** The handle grammar is now shared by producer and
   128	  consumer, the file is rendered through a pipe and written atomically,
   129	  and a truncated CODEOWNERS is recovered from delivery EVIDENCE
   130	  (`cc00235`) — evidence meaning a manifest line that NAMES the path;
   131	  the line's digest grammar is not validated, so keep the manifest
   132	  intact; a CODEOWNERS you switched off survives only a re-run WITHOUT
   133	  `--github-owner` — deleting the file makes the installer render it
   134	  again, and an emptied file with a manifest record is re-rendered too
   135	  (signed condition 61 of rc.1).
   136	- **`uninstall.sh` followed a crafted manifest out of the target.** The
   137	  install manifest is a plain file in your repo and is NOT
   138	  integrity-checked before the removal walk; pre-cure, a record naming
   139	  `../outside/victim.txt` was REMOVED, and with a symlinked `docs`
   140	  component the walk deleted an outside file and the backup archived
   141	  bytes read through the link. Every removal, every backup entry and
   142	  every restore member OUTSIDE `.claude/` is now tested lexically
   143	  (absolute paths, `..` segments, control characters, whitespace and glob
   144	  metacharacters, option-like `-` leaders) and physically (a symlinked
   145	  ancestor under the target) (`6160578`); the `.claude` subtree of a
   146	  restore archive is still extracted whole after a name-only check
   147	  (signed condition 57 of rc.1: restore only unmodified archives this
   148	  uninstaller produced).
   149	- **`doctor.sh` stopped discarding unsafe manifest records in silence** —
   150	  traversal, absolute path, any control byte, symlinked ancestor,
   151	  malformed digest and duplicate relpath are each a NAMED discard, capped
   152	  at 20 and folded into `UNRESOLVED` (rc 1); a manifest containing a NUL
   153	  is refused before the parse (`ba15c71`).
   154	- A fail-closed census of installer write sites
   155	  (`check-installer-write-safety.py`) ships as a RATCHET in `validate.yml`
   156	  with its blind spots declared in the plan, not papered over.
