   158	### Changed — audit log resolves per PROJECT, not per `$HOME` (PLAN-182, ADR-001)
   159	
   160	**Adopter-visible if you run the framework in more than one repository
   161	under the same `$HOME`.** Runtime state — the HMAC audit log, its key,
   162	lock, errors, salt and sidecars — now resolves through one family
   163	resolver (`.claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py`) using Claude Code's own
   164	path-based project slug, instead of a literal `ceo-orchestration`
   165	directory shared by every project (`9de4efc`, `965fb13`, `3d16070`).
   166	
   167	- For repositories with DISTINCT resolved runtime directories, this separates
   168	  their chains and keys and provides correct
   169	  `project` attribution for the emitters that carry the field (a handful
   170	  of newly specified actions still omit `project` or `session_id` and
   171	  cannot be attributed in a shared `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` — rc.1 condition
   172	  23), a `verify_chain()` that means something per project — for stretches
   173	  written by one writer at a time: the previous HMAC is still read before
   174	  the log lock is taken, so two parallel writers can chain to the same
   175	  predecessor and a break is then reported that nobody caused (signed
   176	  condition 67 of rc.1; same order as v1.3.0) — and a per-project HMAC key
   177	  and salt, preventing correlation by `prompt_sha256` between those
   178	  repositories. The path-derived slug can collide: `/srv/a-b/c` and
   179	  `/srv/a/b-c` both yield `-srv-a-b-c`. Verify distinct resolved directories
   180	  before using multiple repositories (rc.1 condition 30); a collision shares
   181	  the log, key and salt. The per-project key is minted on first use and that first
   182	  mint is not exclusive: create it with a single writer before the first
   183	  session (signed condition 68 of rc.1; `docs/UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md`,
   184	  check 11).
   185	- **The old location is not migrated for you.** The pre-v1.4.0 chain
   186	  under `$HOME/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration/` stays where it is;
   187	  `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md` records the change as v2.58 and names the
   188	  legacy path.
   189	- **Plan state and scratchpads move too, and are not migrated either.**
   190	  `state_store.py` resolves through the same family resolver, so a
   191	  repository with an ACTIVE plan on v1.3.0 opens a NEW, empty state
   192	  store after the upgrade — inter-agent handoffs report missing state,
   193	  `/resume` finds no cached graph, while the old SQLite files stay on disk under the
   194	  legacy directory. Two documented routes: set `CEO_PROJECT_NAME` to
   195	  the legacy slug (the explicit escape hatch in `state_store.py`) until
   196	  the plan closes, or copy ONLY `scratchpad/`, `skill_proposals/`,
   197	  `skill_index/` and `session_graph/` from `<legacy>/state/` into
   198	  `<new-runtime-root>/state/`, plus the root-level `session-graphs/` (the
   199	  cached `/resume` graphs; `/resume` otherwise rebuilds from the audit log,
   200	  git and the plan markdown and never reads the stores — sessions recorded
   201	  before the upgrade stay in the legacy chain). The CLI
   202	  `python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py --state-dir` prints
   203	  `<new-runtime-root>`; append `/state` for the store destination.
   204	  NEVER copy the whole legacy `state/` directory or its flat files:
   205	  its audit recovery spools can contaminate the new project's chain.
   206	  First drain or quarantine those spools in the legacy context; follow
   207	  `docs/UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md` and rc.1 condition 27. Automatic migration
   208	  remains a pre-GA follow-up.
   209	- **The limit that does NOT go away:** under the same UID one project's
   210	  process can still read another's `0700` directory and `0600` key. A
   211	  real boundary needs a separate UID; that is out of scope by decision,
   212	  and said here rather than implied away.
   213	- The resolver ships with a CLI
   214	  (`python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py --state-dir|--slug|--project-dir
   215	  [--project PATH]`) used by the pre-push templates and by
   216	  `ceo-backup`/`ceo-restore` (`3d16070`).
