   443	  toggle refuses under CI; the writer script carries a self-path guard
   444	  and the Bash rail carries a best-effort invocation matcher (defense in
   445	  depth — the real boundary is the script's own guard plus the session
   446	  deny surface, and the docs say exactly that, not more).
   447	- **Audited**: every `on`/`off`/refusal emits `night_mode_toggled` into
   448	  the HMAC chain (schema row in `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md`); live-fire
