   456	### Security — sentinel unlock now requires provenance inside git worktrees (ADR-119 Invariant 5)
   457	
   458	- **Adopter-visible tightening of the recovery contract** (SPEC/v1
   459	  `sentinel-format.schema.md` §unlock): inside a git work tree, the
   460	  `CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK` + `CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_ACK` pair alone no longer
   461	  grants — you must also provide provenance via
   462	  `CEO_SESSION_ANCHOR_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)` (captured BEFORE the
   463	  session) **or** `CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_SHA256=<sha256 of approved.md>`.
   464	  The block message teaches both forms when a window is armed. This
   465	  closes a real escalation: during an unlock window the agent could
   466	  author its own `approved.md` (a path guarded by neither rail) and
   467	  self-grant. Classified MINOR under this repo's published policy
   468	  (`VERSIONING.md` §MINOR: "a new trust boundary adopters must
   469	  understand"); MAJOR is reserved for schema-consumer breakage
   470	  (removed/renamed fields, dropped event types), which this is not.
   471	  **Action needed only if you scripted the 2-var unlock inside a git
   472	  worktree** — add one of the two exports above.
