   529	### Changed — install/upgrade semantics (PLAN-166/167/168)
   530	
   531	Adopter-visible behavior of `scripts/install.sh` / `scripts/upgrade.sh`
   532	changed in this release — what a v1.2.0 adopter notices when upgrading:
   533	
   534	- **Ownership is ONE decision, not a cascade (ADR-190).** On upgrade,
   535	  whether the framework owns `PROTOCOL.md`, `SPEC/v1` or
   536	  `.claude/.framework-version` is answered by a single pure decision
   537	  function (`_ownership_verdict()` in
   538	  `scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh`) over the observed ownership
   539	  dimensions — execution-state faults (e.g. a failed backup) stay
   540	  caller-side by design; `upgrade.sh` observes → calls → executes
   541	  instead of deciding locally. Fresh installs sit BEFORE the decision:
   542	  they record the registered delivery (the ADR-155 baseline manifest)
   543	  that upgrade's observations later read. Contract:
   544	  `docs/ownership-decision-table.md`.
   545	- **`SPEC/v1` is a forced route on upgrade.** A framework-owned
   546	  `SPEC/v1` is backed up to `.claude.bak/<timestamp>/SPEC/v1` and
   547	  replaced wholesale — a local edit is a fork of the published
   548	  compliance contract, not a customization. A pre-existing `SPEC/v1`
   549	  with no delivery record is byte-compared against the pristine SPECs
   550	  shipped at v1.2.0 and earlier: a match refreshes it, anything else is
   551	  preserved in place with a named WARNING (ADR-155-AMEND-1). Skipped on
   552	  `--ceremony user` installs.
   553	- **`.claude/.framework-version` is the version marker.** Written on
   554	  install and refreshed on framework-owned, unskipped upgrades;
   555	  `check-framework-updates.sh` and forensic triage read it MARKER-FIRST
   556	  — a well-formed marker validated against its delivery record is the
   557	  signal; an absent, unrecorded, malformed or integrity-failed marker
   558	  falls back to root `VERSION`. The adopter repo's root `VERSION` file
   559	  is deliberately never touched by upgrade — after a framework-owned
   560	  upgrade, the validated marker (not root `VERSION`) is what carries
   561	  the installed framework version.
   562	- **`PROTOCOL.md` pointer has ONE generator.** Install and upgrade
   563	  render the pointer through the same shared generator (byte-identical
   564	  output on both paths); a degraded pointer body is cured with a backup
   565	  and adopter edits are preserved. Skipped on `--ceremony user`
   566	  installs, which never create root files.
   567	
   568	### Fixed — release-verdict readers share ONE fail-closed grammar (PLAN-177)
   569	
   570	The GA re-pass over rc.3 ended NO-GO; the cures landed inside this
   571	train (rc.4) instead of being deferred:
   572	
   573	- **Both release decision gates** — the server-side
   574	  `validate-pair-rail-verdict.py` (step 15) and the local
   575	  `_release_tag_guard.py` (all-modes enforcement) — now parse the
   576	  signed verdict with the same strict ASCII/YAML grammar: indented
   577	  continuations of a scalar, comments glued to the value, Unicode
   578	  whitespace stuck to the token (`GO<U+00A0>` is NOT `GO`) and
   579	  separator-less keys (`verdict:GO`) are each a NAMED rejection, never
   580	  a silent normalization into the authorizing token. Proven by
   581	  cross-reader probe fixtures that run the two rails on every key
   582	  shape and require identical answers.
   583	- **Gitignore delivery is symlink-safe**: the three writers refuse to
   584	  follow a symlinked `.gitignore`/`.claude/.gitignore`, dry-run
   585	  previews print what WOULD be appended (never "asserted clean" over
   586	  debris), and the root-gitignore symlink guard is part of the
   587	  baseline enumeration.
   588	- **plans/ schema docs refresh is hash-gated on upgrade**: only a
   589	  byte-pristine copy of a KNOWN prior framework generation of
   590	  `PLAN-SCHEMA.md`/`DEBATE-SCHEMA.md` is replaced (with backup);
   591	  an adopter-modified schema is PRESERVED loudly. Closes the F3 STALE
   592	  signature the parity e2e flagged. The refresh writes over the
   593	  existing inode (`cp`, not an atomic rename), so a hard link to that
   594	  file outside the target changes with it — signed condition of rc.1:
   595	  no hard links or symlinks anywhere under `.claude/`, `docs/`, `.github/`
   596	  and `SPEC/` before upgrading (two `find` commands in
   597	  `docs/UPGRADE-PROCEDURE.md`; the hook, script, command, skill and
   598	  agent deliveries copy through a link the same way). A `--ceremony
   599	  user` repository upgrades with `--no-settings-migrate` (signed
   600	  condition of rc.1: the leaf migration adds three maintainer-profile
   601	  keys to the advisory profile otherwise).
   602	- **Pre-state ceremony migration fails safe to `user`** and only an
   603	  EXPLICIT `--ceremony` flag / env / recorded state persists into the
   604	  synthesized install-state — the fail-safe inference itself is never
   605	  persisted.
   606	- **npm honesty**: `npm/INTEGRITY.md` names the packlist exceptions
   607	  that actually ship; `SBOM.md`, `install-npm.sh` and `INSTALL.md`
   608	  claims re-verified against behavior.
   609	
   610	### Added — spawn acceptance contract v2 (PLAN-178 Lote B, ADR-191)
   611	
   612	- **FILE ASSIGNMENT grammar with taint semantics** in
   613	  `check_agent_spawn.py`: every named spawn declares `- CAN edit:
   614	  <concrete paths>` or `- CAN edit: NONE-READ-ONLY`; globs, Unicode
   615	  whitespace, control characters or non-whitelisted list lines taint
   616	  the whole declaration. Advisory-first: omission is VISIBLE
   617	  (`spawn_file_assignment_recorded`, `path_count=0`) and the enforce
   618	  flip stays a future ceremony gated on the measure-first window.
   619	- **Fenced + capped inter-agent ingest** in the four shipped Workflow
   620	  skills (byte-identical COMMON block): PROMPT DEFENSE ≥6, explicit
   621	  FILE ASSIGNMENT, anti-spoof fencing with a 24000-char cap whose
   622	  truncation poisons the owning dimension — plus a pre-dispatch
   623	  validator of the reduced ADR-191 grammar in the workflow scripts
   624	  themselves (the Workflow rail does not pass through the spawn hook;
   625	  honest limitation recorded in ADR-191 §4).
   626	- **Shared-memory `query()` returns are fenced**
   627	  (`_lib/memory_shared.py`, ADR-089-AMEND-1) with a derivable
   628	  SEC-P0-02 reopen trigger.
   629	- **Multi-plan budget cap cure** (`check_budget.py`): the previously
   630	  INERT cap (early-allow with ≥2 active plans) now resolves the
